With .NET 10 SDK, you **no longer need `TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport`**. Instead, configure `global.json` with a `test` section:

```json
{
  "sdk": {
    "version": "10.0.100"
  },
  "test": {
    "runner": "Microsoft.Testing.Platform"
  }
}
```

This replaces the per-project `<TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport>true</TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport>` property. The benefit: MTP arguments are passed directly (no `--` separator needed).

Want me to update your project files to use the native .NET 10 approach (remove `TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport` from the csproj and add the `test` section to `global.json`)?
